<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 => \forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 => \forall int i; this.result < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);</code>

Here, `this.result` refers to the return value of the `previousSetBit` method, which is the index of the nearest bit that is set to `true` that occurs on or before the specified starting index. The assertion states that for every index `i` that is greater than the result and less than or equal to `fromIndex`, the bit at index `i` in the `BitSet` is `false`.
--------------------
<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 => \forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);</code>
